# Local agent harness state materialized by .claude/hooks/session-start.sh.
# These hold machine-local settings and secrets and MUST stay out of version
# control. The application-security skill assumes these entries exist; keep them
# (and extend this file with the project's own ignores) during INIT.
/.claude/settings.local.json
.env.local
.env.*.local

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native — generated by `expo prebuild`, not committed
/ios
/android

# scripts/build-native-library.sh's own output — never written to a
# checked-in path; see that script's own header comment.
/.native-build/

# Metro / Jest
.metro-health-check*
*.orig.*

# native build/signing artifacts
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
.kotlin/

# fastlane — reports and downloaded build artifacts, never the lanes
# themselves (fastlane/Fastfile, fastlane/Appfile, fastlane/Pluginfile stay
# committed). See docs/operations/preview-deployment.md.
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/Preview.html
fastlane/screenshots/
fastlane/test_output/
*.keystore
firebase-service-account*.json
*-service-account*.json

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem
npm-debug.*

# Bundler, when a contributor configures a local install path
.bundle/
vendor/bundle/

# Rust — cargo's own build output (433 MB for one debug + release +
# aarch64-linux-android build), never committed.
#
# This entry exists to keep it out of git, and for nothing else. No tool is
# configured to exclude it for speed, because measuring said there was
# nothing to gain: against a populated target/, `eslint .` cost +239 ms on
# ~5.8 s (inside run-to-run noise), `jest` was marginally *faster* with it
# present, and a full project walk cost +3 ms. Prettier skips it anyway, for
# free — its `--ignore-path` defaults to `[.gitignore, .prettierignore]`.
#
# Jest's own `modulePathIgnorePatterns` entry for `modules/*/lib/` is NOT
# part of this: it is a correctness guard, not a speed one. See
# jest.config.js.
modules/*/lib/target/

# modules/espada-engine — its own Android native build's intermediate
# output, never committed. The binaries it ultimately produces
# (android/src/main/jniLibs/**/*.so, ios/EspadaEngine.xcframework) ARE
# meant to be committed, so this only covers what building the module
# locally leaves behind, not the artifacts themselves. iOS build/Pods
# output lands outside modules/ (under the generated, already-ignored
# /ios), so nothing native-iOS-specific is needed here.
modules/espada-engine/android/build/
modules/espada-engine/android/.cxx/
